GPU-style model: 32-lane warps, 32-byte sectors, L2 2 MB 16-way LRU (and 64 MB for comparison), 4-byte elements. MODEL, not a measurement.
[shuffled] = the same at 2 MB with the vertices processed in random order, the worst case for cache locality (a real GPU interleaves thousands of threads; the in-order figure is generous to the GPU, the shuffled one is a ceiling).
waste = DRAM bytes moved by the sector-cache model / IDEAL bytes (each distinct 4-byte word touched, moved once). Lane utilisation: thread-per-vertex (naive) / warp-per-vertex (good libraries).

